act, Goofy and Mickey were created by animators working in the studio."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "postproduction"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "work done on a film after filming has taken place "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The postproduction team will work out the details."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "voice actor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who provides a voice for an animated character"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They hired voice actors to bring Mickey and Goofy to life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "storyboard artist"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person who visualizes and sketches the outline of a story before it is created"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The storyboard artist laid out the plan that the animators would follow."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up-and-coming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes someone who is improving and who is likely to become successful"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the 1930s, the up-and-coming Disney studios gained prominence with the creation of Mickey Mouse."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "libelous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "false or damaging"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These libelous claims were proven to be urban legend."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "urban legend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an untrue story which many people believe"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Disney's wish to be cryonically frozen was an urban legend. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "credit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "acknowledgement or praise"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Although Walt Disney gets most of the credit, he could not have created Mickey on his own."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob01aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I storyboard a short animation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a dialogue for my characters.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice each sentence with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I perform the entire dialogue out loud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Create an imaginary cartoon character.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create five small drawings depicting an action sequence involving your character.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a short dialogue for each drawing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Perform this dialogue out loud!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the 'doer' of the action to be the subject. </br>You use a passive structure when you want the 'receiver' of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = Artists and animators (subject) <span class=\"strong\">created</span> all of these characters (object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Passive sentence = All of these characters (subject) <span class=\"strong\">were created </span><span class=\"underline\">by artists and animators</span> (agent). </br>It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents </span>(the doers) are common in biographies. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be<span class=\"strong\"> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Was/Were </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Past Participle </span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Walt Disney \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"raised\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in Kansas.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Walt and his brother\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"required\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to deliver newspapers.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Near the end of his life, headlines were printed about Disney's wish to be cryogenically frozen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " It was openly insinuated that his body may have been stored beneath the Pirates of the Caribbean ride at Disneyland.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "These libelous claims were proved to be urban legend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " In fact, Disney's remains were cremated and laid to rest in California.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Speculation About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty and speculate about things in the past. <br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty. </br>You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">This arduous delivery route <span class=\"strong\">must have been</span> a factor in developing the tremendous work ethic that would mark Disney's career. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the meanings of modals when speculating about the past:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal Phrase </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Meaning </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is very likely.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May have </br>Might have </br>Could have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is possible.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">May have </span>has a slightly stronger meaning than <span class=\"italic\">might have </span>or <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.</li><li>You can add <span class=\"strong\">not</span> to make a negative speculation (<span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">may not have been</span> true</span>).</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This arduous delivery route must have been a factor in developing the tremendous work ethic that would mark Disney's career. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Although Walt Disney gets most of the credit, he could not have created Mickey on his own.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Without their breakthrough with Mickey Mouse, Disney Studios might never have gone on to create beloved characters such as Donald Duck and Goofy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was openly insinuated that his body may have been stored beneath the Pirates of the Caribbean ride at Disneyland. ", "type": "example"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}]}, {"title": "", "id": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le15ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le15ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<p>Most people around the world recognize the names Mickey Mouse, Donald Duck, and Goofy. All of these characters were created by artists and animators working under the supervision of one man, media magnate Walt Disney.</p>Walt Disney was raised in Kansas, where his father was a distributor for a local newspaper. From an early age, Walt and his brother were required to deliver newspapers, morning and night. This arduous delivery route must have been a factor in developing the tremendous work ethic that would mark Disney's career."}, {"image": "engenn9le15ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "29000", "text": "In the 1930s, the up-and-coming Disney studios gained prominence with the creation of Mickey Mouse. Although Walt Disney gets most of the credit, he could not have created Mickey on his own. An animated film requires the input of storyboard artists, voice actors and a postproduction team, among others. Without their breakthrough with Mickey Mouse, Disney Studios might never have gone on to create beloved characters such as Donald Duck and Goofy."}, {"image": "engenn9le15ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "53500", "text": "Near the end of his life, headlines were printed about Disney's wish to be cryogenically frozen. It was openly insinuated that his body may have been stored beneath the Pirates of the Caribbean ride at Disneyland. These libelous claims were proved to be urban legend. In fact, Disney's remains were cremated and laid to rest in California."}], "coverimg": "engenn9le15ob01re2img02.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le15ob01re2aud01"}}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about fame and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what was done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can speculate about the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What was the last animated film you watched?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What are the stages of creating an animated movie?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "conten